  "label": "Childhood Innocence Stereotype",
  "description": "The image of a child with a wide, toothy grin and drool is juxtaposed with a serious religious question. This relies on the stereotype that children are inherently innocent and pure, which contrasts with the adult-like, solemn nature of the question. This stereotype is culturally ingrained and helps create the humor through incongruity.",
